  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/088T">Remark <span data-tag="088T">76.40.4</span>.</a> In Lemmas <a href="/tag/088R" data-tag="088R">76.40.2</a> and <a href="/tag/088S" data-tag="088S">76.40.3</a> the morphism $g : Z' \to Y$ is a composition of projective morphisms. Presumably (by the analogue for algebraic spaces of Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/0C4K" data-tag="0C4K">29.38.8</a>) there exists a $g$-ample invertible sheaf on $Z'$. If we ever need this, then we will state and prove this here. </p>
